# Auto detect text files and perform LF normalization
* text=auto

# This script is executed by bash inside the archlinux container on CI. Keep it
# LF everywhere: a CR at the end of every line is fatal there (even
# `set -euo pipefail` becomes an invalid option name), and it cannot be caught
# by the YAML parser the way an inline run: block is.
packaging/aur/build-in-container.sh text eol=lf

# Same rule for the release-workflow simulation: it writes its fake `gh` through
# a heredoc, so a CR at the end of every line would be baked into that generated
# script (`exit 0\r` is not a valid exit code) and the simulation would fail in
# a way that has nothing to do with the workflow it is checking. This repo is
# checked out with core.autocrlf=true on Windows, hence the explicit pin.
tools/release-workflow-sim.sh text eol=lf
